            <ArticleTitle>A unique and unexplained ricochet leak post PCI - successfully treated with intra-coronary glue.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>122-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ihj.2013.12.031</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0019-4832(13)00409-4</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We herein describe a unique case of coronary artery perforation treated with covered stent with repeat cardiac tamponade resulting out of a fresh unexplained leak from a remote vessel (Ricochet) and successfully treated with intra-coronary injection of sterile synthetic glue, cyanoacrylate.</AbstractText>
